"The bakery had flour again. On the way to the marsh, Serena passed trays of small loaves cooling in the window. Elric waved, then pointed downstream. He knew this improvement had not happened everywhere.",
"Fen was standing beside a pool that had become too shallow for the nesting shelves. The eggs were safe under damp coverings, ready to move. \"The deeper nursery has room,\" Fen said. \"But it needs shade and a reliable water supply.\"",
"Dribble carried empty baskets to the dry path. He did not touch the eggs. Fen would do that part; helpers could prepare the receiving pool and bring clean water. Another possibility was to lend the marsh a small mill turn while a shaded basin was prepared. That would delay the next flour batch.",
"\"I thought the bread would make this feel finished,\" Serena admitted. \"It finished one job,\" Lucas said. \"Here is another.\"",
"Fen was not asking her to erase the council decision. The guardian wanted her to help with the cost she had understood when she made it. There was room for more than one repair, but no repair that required only a speech."
