"Elric reached the gate carrying a half-filled grain measure. Fen arrived with a water stick. Both pointed to the schedule. Both had followed it. Both looked annoyed.",
"The mill needed a little longer to finish its last batch before the gate turned. The marsh had dipped too low near the end of its dry interval. A schedule that looked fair on paper had overlooked what happened between its neat lines.",
"\"I thought sharing would stop the argument,\" Serena said. \"It shared the waiting,\" Lucas replied. \"That is useful, but different.\" Dribble offered to divide a biscuit as an example. Unfortunately, he had already eaten most of it.",
"They could work a day of measured handovers together, letting actual water depth signal when a turn must end. That asked both sides to provide a watcher. Or they could test a simpler, longer rotation over two days, with fewer trips to the gate but longer waits for each side.",
"Neither plan would give everyone full flow. Each could replace an irritating surprise with an understood agreement. Serena put down the schedule and asked Elric and Fen to show her the measurements that their earlier meeting had missed."
};

