"For longer turns, they would test a simpler rotation over two days. There would be fewer journeys to the gate, but the bakery would make flour in larger batches and the nursery helpers would carry extra water between marsh turns. The waiting would be more predictable, not shorter.",
"Dribble suggested announcing every handover with a soup spoon on a pot. Lucas suggested a written sign instead. The pot's owner strongly supported Lucas.",
"Serena read both plans aloud. This was not a contest to find the cleverest compromise. It was a choice about which inconvenience people could manage, followed by enough work to discover whether they had been right."
