"The bakery window held a fresh row of loaves. Elric was busy enough to complain about being busy, which Serena suspected was an improvement. He still checked the river gauge before promising the next batch.",
"Downstream, Fen's shaded nursery held the eggs safely. Some surrounding paths remained dry. The deeper pool required visits and carrying, and the reed cover needed mending where the wind worried its edge. The marsh had gained helpers rather than all its old water.",
"Serena stopped to ask what was needed next. Fen showed her a short list instead of starting the old argument. Elric sent bread for the people doing the checks. Neither action made them agree about the original decision. It did make the next day's work easier to arrange.",
"Lucas kept the journal open to unfinished tasks. If the bridge still needed attention, its entry remained there. Supplies and unkept promises stayed in their own words. Chapter One was complete without turning every loose end into a victory ribbon.",
"Dribble studied the northern messenger's note. \"Do highland gates have kitchens?\" Serena folded the map. \"We will have to ask.\" For now, Willowbrook remained open to visit."
};

